  "question": {
    "text": "Consider an ideal gas confined in an isolated closed chamber. As the gas undergoes an adiabatic expansion, the average time of collision between molecules increases as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></math> , where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> is the volume of the gas. The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> is:<br />\r<br />\r<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>"
